<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζηλ-ωτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Andr.</u>
			5
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Med.</u>
			1035
		</span></i>; 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζᾱλ-</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Simon.
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
		</span></i>(v. infr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>enviable</i>, of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Hp.Mi.</u>
					368b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλὰ καὶ ζ. ἐπιγράμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					22.72
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				6.95
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζηλωτὸν ὁ πλοῦτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lycurg.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					97
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be deemed happy, to beenvied</i>, of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				455
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1161
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> by one, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				710
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1035
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				197d
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					5.69
				</span></i>
			: c.gen. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆκέ μιν ζαλωτὸν ὁμόφρονος εὐνᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					7.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ. τῆς εὐνοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					61
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Luc.</u>
				38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of
			conditions, <i>enviable, blessed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					71
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				243
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πότμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					675
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζηλωτότατος βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					464
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.289b
				</span></i>
			, etc.</div>
